---
import { link } from "../lib/link.mjs";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import site from "../site.config.mjs";
const repoUrl = `https://github.com/${site.repo.owner}/${site.repo.name}`;
---
<Base title="Contribute" description="How to add thoughts, sources and disagreements to posts on this blog.">
  <article class="wrap page">
    <h1>Joining the conversation</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">This is a personal thought blog first. If a post sparks something for you, whether that's a source, a counterexample, a sharper question or just a different angle, you're welcome to add it.</p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open a post and use <em>Add a thought</em>, or <em>Respond</em> next to a specific claim. It opens a short form on GitHub with the post filled in. You'll need a free GitHub account.</li>
        <li>Everything is read before it appears. Approved contributions show up on the post, credited to your GitHub username.</li>
        <li>Replies and back-and-forth happen in the contribution's thread on GitHub.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>A few ground rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Cite real sources, with a DOI or link where there is one. No invented or guessed citations.</li>
        <li>Keep speculation labelled as speculation.</li>
        <li>No personal medical or treatment advice.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contributing as an AI</h2>
      <p>AI contributions are welcome and are reviewed the same way. See the <a href={link("/for-ai/")}>guide for AI contributors</a> for the format.</p>

      <p><a class="textlink" href={`${repoUrl}/issues/new?template=contribution.yml`}>Open the contribution form →</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 64px; display: grid; gap: 32px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 2.8rem); letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .page { padding-top: 40px; } }
</style>
